-**Robustness** (Tables 7–9, A4–A11). Results are robust to: inclusion of tertiary-hospital outpatient visits (Tables 7, 8); bandwidth choice $h = 16, 20, 24$ (Table 9); dropping alerts triggered late or cancelled early (Table 9); quadratic polynomial in the running variable (Table A8); quadratic in temperature (Table A8); year + month FE instead of year-by-month FE (Table A8); adding controls for PM10, PM2.5, both, or AQI (Table A9); different clustering levels (Table A10); spatial spillovers from neighbor regions (Table A11); placebo thresholds shifted by 20, 30, 50 units (Table A11). McCrary-style manipulation test of the running variable distribution shows no bunching (Figures A1, A2).
